  runs.run('fp4-gemv-pairs', {agent: 'worker', task: 'Candidate 2 — grouped FP4 decode GEMV with pair-list dispatch. You are analyzing a porting candidate for the vkernels repo (cwd). Reference implementation: /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cuda/fp4_gemv.cu (fp4_gemv_pairs: grouped E2M1 expert decode GEMV, pair-list dispatch row_in/expert/wt, activation staged in shared memory TRANSPOSED xs[j][c] = x[32c+j] so 32 lanes read consecutive addresses with no bank conflicts, 16-entry E2M1 shared LUT, fp32 accum, one output per (pair,n), no atomics, K<=5120) and its wrapper in /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cukern.py. OUR SIDE: src/python/vkernels/torch_ops/v41_mxfp4_gemv.py (Triton mxfp4_expert_gemv, plain per-row GEMV), src/c/vkernels/kernels/glm_moe.{hpp,hip} (glm_expert_gemv fp8 split-K with gemv_pick_sk tuning), src/c/vkernels/kernels/moe_device.hip. QUESTION: what do we gain from the pair-list + transposed-smem + no-atomics schedule vs our current v41_mxfp4_gemv, and is it worth a HIP/CUDA port? Note our repo's tuning-store pattern (bench_glm_fp8_gemv --persist, gemv_pick_sk) as the integration path. Identify the exact launch geometry (grid (N/rows_per_block, n_pairs), block 256, 8 warps x 4 rows) and smem footprint as a function of K. WRITE your plan to docs/candidates/dsv41-fp4-gemv-pairs.md (create dir). Do not modify any other file. Return a 10-line summary.'),
  runs.run('group-split-routing', {agent: 'worker', task: 'Candidate 3 — adaptive small/large group routing for grouped MoE. You are analyzing a porting candidate for the vkernels repo (cwd). Reference implementation: /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cuda/fp4_tc.cu (grouped FP4 mma GEMM for small groups, <=16 tokens, expert re-read per tile) and /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cuda/fp4_tcw.cu (operand-flipped layout for large groups up to 64 tokens: weights as mma A operand, tokens as B, expert read ONCE per group, cp.async STAGES-deep activation tiles, groups outside [min_tok,max_tok] skipped, zero_out mode for other GPUs EP shards), plus the launcher logic in /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cukern.py and /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/moe_kernels.py (GroupedPairs, grouped_fp4_gemm, grouped_fp4_gemm_chunked). OUR SIDE: src/c/vkernels/kernels/moe_fused.{hpp,hip} (single fixed two-stage schedule) and NOTES-fusion-moe-align-device.md / NOTES-157.md for our current MoE aux fusion work. QUESTION: would adaptive small-group/large-group kernel routing help our fused MoE decode shapes, and how does the operand-flip (weights-as-A) schedule map to CDNA MFMA? Quantify the expert re-read amplification both ways for typical decode EP loads (e.g. 384 experts, top-k 8, batch 1..64 across 5 GPUs). WRITE your plan to docs/candidates/dsv41-group-split-routing.md (create dir). Do not modify any other file. Return a 10-line summary.'),
  runs.run('push-allreduce', {agent: 'worker', task: 'Candidate 4 — push-style one-shot all-reduce for small decode vectors. You are analyzing a porting candidate for the vkernels repo (cwd). Reference implementation: /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cuda/allreduce.cu — push-style ONE-SHOT all-reduce for small bf16 vectors across P2P-connected GPUs, single process, no NCCL: per-GPU buf[W][n] and flags[W] plus seq counter; three graph-capturable kernels (ar_push: P2P-store x into every peer row; ar_signal: threadfence_system, set peer flags, spin until own flags==seq; ar_reduce: sum rows). Also see /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/cuda/p2p.cu for the flag/signal convention. OUR SIDE: src/c/vkernels/comm/allreduce.{hpp,cpp,cu} (ring all-reduce over channels), src/c/vkernels/comm/topology.{hpp,cpp}, src/c/vkernels/comm/pipeline_boundary.{hpp,cpp,cu} (graph-capturable PP boundary, issue #10), docs/comm-rccl.md. QUESTION: our ring is bandwidth-optimal but latency-poor for decode-sized messages; would a push one-shot AR complement it (latency-optimized small-message path, e.g. hidden=7168 bf16 = 14KB vectors)? Design the integration: where it slots into our channel/topology abstractions, our two-implementation model (CPU mock backend must stay testable GPU-less), CUDA-graph capture rules (we document them for pipeline_boundary — same constraints apply), and how it would extend to HIP/RCCL (rccl vs hand-rolled xGMI stores on MI300A). WRITE your plan to docs/candidates/dsv41-push-allreduce.md (create dir). Do not modify any other file. Return a 10-line summary.'),
