  runs.run('fused-quant-epilogues', {agent: 'worker', task: 'Candidate 6 — fused SwiGLU/RMSNorm + FP8-quant epilogues. You are analyzing a porting candidate for the vkernels repo (cwd). Reference implementation: /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/fused.py (swiglu_quant: SwiGLU with clamp + FP8 e4m3/E8M0 block quant + optional 8-row mma permutation in ONE Triton kernel; norm_quant; hc_pre_norm_quant / hc_pre_norm_quant2: RMSNorm + quant fused, optionally after hyper-connection mix) and /tmp/dsv41/dsv41/fused2.py. OUR SIDE: src/python/vkernels/torch_ops/aiter_ops.py — note lines ~270-500: we run grouped fp8-blockscale MoE with a STAGE SPLIT and apply floe clamp-swiglu in torch BETWEEN GEMM stages because aiter in-kernel SwiGLU cannot express the clamp — that is an explicit extra read+write round-trip of the [EM, 2*ispp] intermediate; also src/python/vkernels/torch_ops/elementwise.py, glm_expert_gather_dequant.py, and docs/kernels/moe_aux.md + NOTES-155/156/157.md (our fusion-candidate process: rank candidates, write a NOTES-xxx.md with baseline, roofline, plan). QUESTION: quantify the DRAM traffic our current stage-split pays vs a fused act+quant epilogue for our W4A4/W8A8 grouped GEMM shapes (hidden 7168, ispp 2048 typical), decide Triton vs HIP placement, and check numerics: does one-pass fused quant change results vs our current two-pass (per-group ue8m0 scales computed in sorted-row order)? Follow our NOTES-155 format and write your analysis+plan to docs/candidates/dsv41-fused-quant-epilogues.md (create dir). Do not modify any other file. Return a 10-line summary.'),
]);
return plans.map((p, i) => ({candidate: ['tc-gemm-family','fp4-gemv-pairs','group-split-routing','push-allreduce','p2p-ep-dispatch','fused-quant-epilogues'][i], summary: p.output}));

